bject keys: ['forbidden_visible_terms', 'internal_fields', 'preferred_terms', 'run_unit', 'threshold_rate_rule', 'variant_unit']\nresults_dir work/results/r02/codex/20261117_111421/investigation\ntop_programs list count: 3 first item: {'attempt_dir_name': 'idea_root', 'attempt_id': 'cycle_03_rank_calibrated_scale_selection_attempt_01', 'combined_score': 0.6450635814905741, 'correct': True, 'eligible': True, 'eval_index': 3, 'evaluation_evidence': {'candidate_diagnostics_trust': 'unverified', 'episode_count': 3, 'episodes': [{'correct': True, 'duration_seconds': 7.21525754313916, 'score': 0.6351655813211198, 'seed': 17, 'solution': {'cases': [{'case': 'LN_IID_K3', 'complete': True, 'control_checks': {'constant_input': True, 'copy_point': True, 'permuted_input': True, 'reset_unfitted': True}, 'controls': ['constant_input', 'copy_point', 'permuted_input', 'reset_unfitted'], 'methods': {'bonferroni': [{'alpha': 0.05, 'conditional_wilson95': [0.9166653321421131, 0.9472811377919342], 'coverage': 0.93359375, 'coverage_error': \ntotals object keys: ['attempts', 'correct_programs', 'evaluated_programs', 'ideas']\n\npaper_strategy.json\nstatus ready\nselected_prompt_family paper_standalone\nrecommended_title Scale-Adaptive Compositional Conformal Regions: Reliability and Limits\ncentral_question Across the tested synthetic response distributions, dimensions, and covariate regimes, how do training-only scale-adaptive ILR conformal regions trade observed-composition coverage against uniform-simplex region mass relative to matched-center alternatives?\ncentral_thesis In the six tested synthetic settings, scale-adaptive ILR regions exhibit condition-dependent reliability–efficiency trade-offs rather than uniform dominance: near-target IID coverage coexists with shifted Dirichlet undercoverage, and higher aggregate utility does not imply smaller simplex regions or conditional validity.\nnarrative_rationale The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation with eight seed blocks, paired region constructions, three nominal coverage levels, and explicit coverage, reference-mass, and uncertainty records. It supports a bounded empirical study, not a search-success narrative or a causal claim that rank-based selection improves performance. The IID Dirichlet K=8 comparison and the shifted Dirichlet reversals supply complementary evidence for one thesis. Final qualification is independently recorded as completed/qualified/true; this administrative outcome does not certify scientific generality. No downstream_study is present.\nprior_paper_story_status recentered\nedit_framing_decision No edit context, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated bundle, or extra_tasks bundle is staged, so there is no prior manuscript to preserve or rewrite. Recentered denotes narrowing the broad source-task motivation and earlier proposed geometry audit to the actually evaluated fixed-ILR scale-adaptation study. Do not imply that an earlier paper was revised.\nstaged_input_impact list count: 6 first item: The final evaluator evidence, rather than qualitative memory, sets the main paper scope: logistic-normal IID, Dirichlet IID, and shifted Dirichlet responses, each at K=3 and K=8.\nmethod_groups list count: 5 first item: {'name': 'Training-only scale-adaptive ILR regions', 'role': 'proposed', 'include_reason': 'The frozen studied configuration: fixed-basis ridge centers, positive diagonal base scales, shrunk scalar local-moment correction, training-only rank-volume selection, and independent pooled split calibration. Proposed denotes the studied configuration, not proven novelty or superiority of its selector.'}\nresults_focus list count: 8 first item: Use only final.evidence.episodes for the principal comparisons: eight seeds, six conditions, and nominal coverage 0.95, 0.90, and 0.80. Present the six conditions as a shared design with condition-specific limits, not successive experiments.\nfigure_plan list count: 3 first item: Figure 1, early conceptual overview: training-only scale selection, independent calibration, and two distinct evaluation axes; explicitly distinguish the ILR surrogate from simplex reference mass.\nfigure_specs list count: 3 first item: {'figure_id': 'composition_reliability_overview', 'required': True, 'purpose': 'Make the prediction target, training/calibration separation, scale-selection mechanism, and distinct reliability/efficiency estimands legible at a glance.', 'figure_type': 'diagram', 'preferred_generator': 'generate-concept-figure', 'group_by': 'scientific_stage_not_search_order', 'metric': 'observed-composition membership and uniform-simplex reference mass', 'split_by': 'training-only fitting, independent calibration, evaluation', 'preferred_span': 'full_width', 'target_width_fraction': 0.98, 'target_height_inches': 1.6, 'layout_rationale': 'The ICLR text column is the full 5.5-inch text width. A three-part horizontal overview at about 5.39 inches wide and 1.6 inches high allows short labels at 9–10 pt; do not\nsupplementary_plan object keys: ['purpose', 'planned_subsections']\nforbidden_headings list count: 9 first item: Search Progression\nforbidden_phrases list count: 17 first item: correctness rate\nnotes_for_writer list count: 22 first item: Use a thesis-first standalone structure: Introduction; Related Work; Prediction Regions and Evaluation Targets; Training-only Scale Adaptation; Experimental Design and Uncertainty; Reliability–Efficiency Results; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. These are scientific sections, not implementation or discovery chronology.\nfailure_reason \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
