{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"tail -n 35 memory.md; ls global_memory/conclusions.md global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py 2>/dev/null; sed -n '1,130p' .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py; command -v apply_patch; git status --short 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"### 2026-11-17T13:12:18.341797+00:00 | step=idea | scope=paper\n- summary: Independent final and venue evidence inspected; framing candidates are a selection mechanism paper, a reliability-efficiency audit, or a broad geometry story. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No new evaluation or mechanism evidence has been generated.\n- evidence: final.qualification.status/outcome/correct report completed/qualified/true, independently of absent downstream_study. Eight final seeds, six synthetic conditions, three alpha levels and seed-block paired uncertainty are present. No edit context or previous manuscript exists. paper.sty supplies a single 5.5-inch text column. The first memory helper call appended locally but rejected the global_memory symlink; this retry uses its resolved path.\n- next_action: Inspect controlled comparisons and training-only selection implementation, then select a qualified thesis without causal or universal superiority claims.\n\n### 2026-11-17T13:20:01.977691+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Choose a thesis-first reliability-efficiency audit of frozen scale-adaptive ILR regions; reject causal selector superiority and unimplemented broad geometry/Mondrian stories. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=This frames existing evaluated evidence rather than adding or strengthening a methodological recommendation.\n- evidence: final.metric.iid_coverage_error=0.013562011718750005; final.metric.shift_coverage_error=0.13034261067708333; final.metric.baseline_utility_gap=0.011594669497844157. Evaluator method records show mean simplex mass 0.3034934467739529 for scaled ILR versus 0.2917009546491835 for simplex L-infinity, despite higher aggregate utility. Condition comparisons show gains concentrated in IID Dirichlet K=8 and losses against simplex controls under shift. Stored paired intervals exist; uncertainty objects repeat across episode wrappers and must be deduplicated. Final selector-specific ablation and original-initializer final results are absent. Shift expands covariate support; its mechanisms are not isolated.\n- next_action: Write mirrored strategy files with three readable figures, substantive 8-9 page plan, supplementary source ledger, final qualification disclosure, and strict search/final separation.\n\n### 2026-11-17T13:21:10.084111+00:00 | step=verify | scope=paper\n- summary: Strategy-only checks passed for both required outputs. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Structural and grounding verification supplies no new scientific evaluation and does not strengthen the existing methodological conclusions.\n- evidence: paper_strategy.json parses and has all required fields; its source IDs exist in paper_data.json and referenced local paths exist. Three required figures satisfy panel/category/series budgets, exactly one uses generate-concept-figure, all have single-column ICLR layout rationales. Seven supplementary entries match the Markdown memo. Final qualification, eight-seed/six-condition completeness, repeated uncertainty-object identity, final utility/comparator gap, and 8.6-page allocation were checked. Neither paper.tex nor claims_grounding.json was created; no final-paper validator, research experiment, literature browsing, or figure generator was run.\n- next_action: Pass the ready strategy to the standalone writer; implement plots from retained final measurements, preserve shift failures and qualification boundaries, and verify relevant bibliography sources before citing.\n\n### 2026-11-17T13:21:10.131682+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper_strategy_ready: wrote paper_strategy.md and paper_strategy.json with a bounded reliability-efficiency thesis instead of a search diary. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The framing preserves available findings and uncertainty without new causal or superiority claims.\n- evidence: Chosen audit framing beats an unimplemented broad geometry story and an unsupported selector-superiority story. It retains unfavorable baseline comparisons and shifted undercoverage, reports the independently grounded qualified final outcome, omits unsupported original-initializer/campaign accounting, and plans three readable figures plus substantive post-reference methods, comparison, diagnostic, provenance and LLM-use material. Existing distilled text calling rank selection untested remains stale private context and was not propagated into the strategy.\n- next_action: Later writing should test only what can be derived from the retained evaluator evidence and disclose missing matched final selector/initializer comparisons; no additional scientific result is implied by strategy completion.\n\n### 2026-11-17T13:23:55.368676+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Writer adopts controlled reliability–efficiency audit; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No new scientific evaluation is introduced.\n- evidence: Independent final qualification is completed/qualified/true; no downstream_study or task_names; six synthetic cases and eight seeds. Source exposes nested training-only rank selection, not Mondrian or alternative geometries. Existing bibliography contains unrelated clinical/application hits and needs targeted replacement before citation.\n- next_action: Archive inspectable evaluated source, derive figures only from final records, retrieve exact known foundational references with forbidden-content safeguards, draft and validate.\n\n### 2026-11-17T13:48:01.343998+00:00 | step=verify | scope=paper\n- summary: Draft and retained-data plots written; 96 mapped claims pass grounding and 25 consulted references pass citation checks; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Derived descriptive intervals refine reporting without establishing a new method recommendation.\n- evidence: IID/shift coverage errors remain .013562/.130343. Paired aggregate simplex-baseline utility difference .011595 with descriptive seed-bootstrap [.004738,.017943] is reported alongside larger mass .303493 versus .291701 and every unfavorable shifted contrast. Rejected unrelated bibliography hits, wrong DOI matches and selector-causal framing. Scientific verifier currently has zero dangling refs. SI tables were embedded to satisfy source checks. Canonical figure helper cannot import unavailable src; canonical compile input gate rejects a system texmf.cnf symlink between approved system trees. Independent schema/render checks are being prepared; these environment issues will not be hidden.\n- next_action: Complete rendered-page, reference and source-line checks, finalize reproducibility and provenance, rerun grounding; leave required conceptual image for synchronous orchestrator rendering.\n\n### 2026-11-17T14:10:53.832334+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: paper.tex and claims_grounding.json are consistent with grounded inputs; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The final manuscript preserves the evaluated scope and adds no new mechanism-level recommendation.\n- evidence: Authored and compiled a nine-page main body with references and substantive embedded supplement; mapped 102 claims and 25 consulted references; three quantitative composite figures plus orchestrator-owned overview placeholder are registered. Canonical section/citation, claim-grounding and rendered-SI checks pass; scientific-evidence verification has zero dangling links. Independent canonical-schema, figure-density, numeric-consistency, source-copy and rendered-input checks pass. No new research evaluation was run and paper_data.json was not edited. Final qualification is independently completed/qualified/true; shifted undercoverage and unfavorable mass/utility contrasts remain visible. Readable evaluated sources are archived. Canonical figure-wrapper import and compiler system-symlink limitations are explicitly recorded in validation_report.json, not reported as passed.\n- next_action: Orchestrator should synchronously replace the guarded conceptual placeholder, compile again, and perform authoritative final layout checks; no further scientific claim is implied by this handoff.\n\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\nglobal_memory/conclusions.md\nglobal_memory/memory.jsonl\nglobal_memory/memory.md\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Append validated local/global memory entries for idea workflows.\n\nTwo modes:\n\n* default (event append) — appends one memory event to ``memory.md`` (local +\n  global) plus one JSONL record to ``memory.jsonl``. Existing behavior.\n* ``--write-conclusions`` — atomically replaces ``conclusions.md`` with a\n  validated single-paragraph distilled summary and appends a record to\n  ``conclusions_history.jsonl``. Validation rejects empty input,\n  multi-paragraph input, or input over 300 words.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport fcntl\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nCONCLUSIONS_WORD_LIMIT = 300\nGATE_TRIGGER_VALUES = (\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\")\n\nLOCAL_MEMORY_HEADERS = \"\"\"# Memory Log\n\n## Context\n## Idea Discoveries\n## Program Evaluations\n## Failures / Regressions\n## Next Hypotheses\n\"\"\"\n\nGLOBAL_MEMORY_HEADER = \"# Global Memory Log\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef utc_now() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the current UTC timestamp string.\"\"\"\n    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n\n\ndef _load_event(*, event_json: str | None, event_file: Path | None) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Load event.\"\"\"\n    if event_json:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_json)\n    elif event_file is not None:\n        parsed = json.loads(event_file.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    else:\n        raw = input().strip()\n        if not raw:\n            raise ValueError(\"missing event payload\")\n        parsed = json.loads(raw)\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"event payload must be a JSON object\")\n    return parsed\n\n\ndef _ensure_required_fields(event: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    \"\"\"Ensure required fields.\"\"\"\n    normalized = dict(event)\n    if not isinstance(normalized.get(\"timestamp\"), str) or not normalized[\"timestamp\"].strip():\n        normalized[\"timestamp\"] = utc_now()\n\n    required_string_fields = (\"step\", \"scope\", \"summary\", \"evidence\", \"next_action\")\n    for key in required_string_fields:\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if not isinstance(value, str) or not value.strip():\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing required string field: {key}\")\n        normalized[key] = value.strip()\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = normalized.get(key)\n        if value is None:\n            continue\n        if not isinstance(value, str):\n            normalized[key] = str(value)\n        normalized[key] = normalized[key].strip() or None\n\n    metrics = normalized.get(\"metrics\")\n    if metrics is not None and not isinstance(metrics, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"metrics must be an object when present\")\n    rubrics = normalized.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if rubrics is not None and not isinstance(rubrics, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"rubrics must be an array when present\")\n    tags = normalized.get(\"tags\")\n    if tags is not None:\n        if not isinstance(tags, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"tags must be an array when present\")\n        normalized[\"tags\"] = [str(item).strip() for item in tags if str(item).strip()]\n    return normalized\n\n\ndef _markdown_entry(event: dict[str, Any]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Handle markdown entry logic for this module.\"\"\"\n    lines = [\n        f\"### {event['timestamp']} | step={event['step']} | scope={event['scope']}\",\n        f\"- summary: {event['summary']}\",\n        f\"- evidence: {event['evidence']}\",\n        f\"- next_action: {event['next_action']}\",\n    ]\n\n    for key in (\"idea_id\", \"attempt_id\", \"program_id\"):\n        value = event.get(key)\n        if isinstance(value, str) and value.strip():\n            lines.append(f\"- {key}: {value.strip()}\")\n\n    metrics = event.get(\"metrics\")\n    if isinstance(metrics, dict) and metrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- metrics: {json.dumps(metrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    rubrics = event.get(\"rubrics\")\n    if isinstance(rubrics, list) and rubrics:\n        lines.append(f\"- rubrics: {json.dumps(rubrics, sort_keys=True)}\")\n    tags = event.get(\"tags\")\n    if isinstance(tags, list) and tags:\n        lines.append(f\"- tags: {', '.join(str(item) for item in tags)}\")\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\\n\"\n\n\ndef _append_text(path: Path, text: str, *, header: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Safely initialize and append text to a regular file.\"\"\"\n    fd = _open_regular_for_append(path)\n    try:\n        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\n        size = os.fstat(fd).st_size\n        if not size:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
